- Code formatting
    - PEP-8 except for:
        - No spaces around *, /, //, or **
        - One space on each side of +, -, %
        - One space on each side of &, |, <<, >>, <, <=, >, >=, !=, ==, 'or', and 'and'
        - No blank lines in file except if put into docstrings
    - Important:  please make sure to put a newline after a ':' in a conditional, class
      or function definition, as lacking it makes it very easy to miss the logic when
      reading
    - Triple quotes: use ''' for all docstrings and multi-line strings.
    - Quotes:  use " for all string definitions, such as 'a = "a string"'.
    - Naming:  CamelCase naming for classes and functions, snake case for attributes and
      local variables
    - Use 'import x' if possible.  Then us x.y notation in code.  'import x as y' is
      fine too.
    - Folding blocks:  use 'if 1:  # Comment' to group code for folding editors.  This
      also allows for easy runtime toggling.
    - Type annotations:  use type annotations wherever possible
- Remind me to check the repository commit state before making significant changes
- Much to most of the time, supply all the code we're working on, as it's too difficult
  to piece things into an existing file (particularly when I'm tired).  Thus, try to
  give me the whole class or whole function we're working on.
- ASCII characters: use plain ASCII wherever possible.  Avoid Unicode punctuation like
  em-dashes, single and double fancy quotes, etc.

